      "parent_visual": {
        "decision": "Retain bounded stylized relief candidate, preserving repetitive basalt texture, regular stepped terrain and rigid curtain-water caveats. Not photoreal marketing or final user approval.",
        "hardware": "Brass clasp, round fitting, ring and caps contrast clearly against dark shell; simplified blocky finish and mobile shadowed feet limit detail. Released open latch is expected, with no visible evidence requiring a detached-part diagnosis.",
        "limitations": "Reviewed original desktop/mobile closed/open captures and marketing.webp, plus supplied source notes/brief where available. Static images do not certify motion, hidden attachments, exact pigment, physical-phone performance or manufacture. Technical checks were supplied, not rerun. No final user visual approval. Shared Zambia/Zimbabwe landscape, not exclusively Zambian or a scale geological reconstruction. Dark lower edges blend into background on mobile and supporting UI text is small.",
        "quality": "Recognizable basalt/gorge chest with turquoise channel and white waterfall in both closed views; all open silhouettes fit. Marketing has stronger grain/contact shading, but shares the same clearly sculptural treatment.",
        "terrain": "Raised stepped banks flank upper water and rigid ribbed white drop into lower channel. Sparse pebble-like greenery and broad planar rocks are schematic. No obvious unsupported water edge in these views; lower channel is between raised banks, not cut through lid. Open front view hides lid-top terrain normally.",
        "texture": "Repetitive wavy gray-green striations across body and interior read as carved/painted or woodgrain-like rather than natural basalt. Water is opaque rigid relief without mist, translucency or hydrodynamics; marketing also has these stylized limits."
      },
